<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">J. B. M. Hertzog</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as James Barry Munnik Hertzog, Barry Hertzog</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">J. B. M. Hertzog was a South African lawyer, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> general and politician. A judge in the Orange Free State before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>, he led commandos during its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> phase, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-south-africa">National Party</a> in 1914 and was prime minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> from 1924 to 1939, promoting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaner</a> interests. He resigned when parliament voted to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/j-b-m-hertzog.jpg" alt="J. B. M. Hertzog" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bain News Service, publisher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:JBM_Hertzog_-_SA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
